  "title": "French and European Supermarket Cyberattacks Trigger Food Losses and Fires",
  "summary": "Hundreds of French and European supermarkets were targeted by hackers, causing food spoilage, fires, and significant financial losses, as reported by The Guardian World and BBC World News. A second cyberattack targeting supermarket refrigeration systems in Europe led to similar incidents, with temperatures reaching up to 50°C in some cases.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "French and European supermarkets were targeted by hackers, causing food spoilage and triggering fires.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "A second cyberattack targeting supermarket refrigeration systems in Europe led to similar incidents with temperatures reaching up to 50°C.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The French foreign minister blamed Iran for orchestrating the attacks, claiming it was an act of unprecedented scale and aggression.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
